<p>To conditionally install the <a href="">swag</a> command required for my
<code>openapi-generate</code> target, I find this approach to be both easy and
portable. It works well because <code>swag</code> is a Go binary, so I have a way
to install it regardless of the user's platform, using <code>go install</code>:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>GOPATH<span class="w"> </span>?<span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">$(</span>HOME<span class="k">)</span>/go/bin
<span class="nv">SWAG</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">$(</span>GOPATH<span class="k">)</span>/swag
openapi-generate:
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nb">test</span><span class="w"> </span>-x<span class="w"> </span><span class="k">$(</span>SWAG<span class="k">)</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">||</span><span class="w"> </span>go<span class="w"> </span>install<span class="w"> </span>github.com/swaggo/swag/cmd/swag
<span class="w">    </span><span class="k">$(</span>SWAG<span class="k">)</span><span class="w"> </span>init
<span class="w">    </span><span class="k">$(</span>SWAG<span class="k">)</span><span class="w"> </span>fmt
</code></pre></div>

<p>It's important to note, the variables must be set <em>outside</em> the
target, <code>openapi-generate</code>.</p>